Dear Ms. Wiggins,

I'm reaching out from the Durham County Health Department. We've been hearing reports of respiratory issues among farmworkers in the eastern part of the county -- seems to be related to the heavy dust this season with the dry spell we've had.

I know you have a background in traditional herbalism and I've heard great things about the work you're doing with the Deep Roots program. Several of the affected workers are from the communities you serve.

Would you be willing to officially recommend specific herbal preparations that would help with these respiratory symptoms? We could include your recommendations in the health advisory we're preparing for distribution to farming communities.

Any guidance you can provide would be much appreciated. These folks need help and the conventional options are limited for many of them.

Thank you,
